From ea2b461ad8d7b52b6870750f27609949ad3c907b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:50:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support pydantic v1.10.x (pure-Python, no Rust) alongside v2

pydantic v1 has two semantics that no shim can hide, so the option
models avoid them at the type-definition level:

- A Union validates first-match-wins with coercion, whereas v2 tries
  an exact type match first. PathOrIO (BinaryIO | IOBase | Path | str |
  bytes) therefore turned the '-' stdin/stdout sentinel into a Path, and
  plugins: Sequence[Path | str] turned plugin module names into Paths
  that the loader then treated as files. PathOrIO now uses a validating
  instance_of() type under v1, and the plugins union is ordered str |
  Path (harmless under v2).
- An Any-typed field is implicitly optional under v1, so Any is not
  a usable fallback for the required input_file/output_file.

user_words/user_patterns were typed os.PathLike, which v2 coerces from
str but v1 treats as an arbitrary type with a strict isinstance check;
they are now Path.

The shim raises NotImplementedError for ConfigDict keys and validator
modes it does not map, so a rebase that starts using more of the v2 API
fails at import under v1 instead of silently degrading. pydantic v1 does
re-run root validators on assignment under validate_assignment, so the
mode='after' emulation also covers attribute assignment.

tests/test_pydantic_compat.py pins the invariants both majors must
satisfy; the wording of pydantic's own constraint messages differs
between majors, so two existing tests match more loosely. The
option-related test subset has identical pass/fail sets under pydantic
1.10.26 and 2.13.5 on Python 3.12, and under 1.10.26 on Python 3.14.

